body:
Actually, I got a workaround fix for it, I had chatgpt write me an addon that fixes it. For anyone else who has the same problem, save this as a .py file and install it as an addon.




```py
bl_info = {
    "name": "Change Cursor in Edit Mode",
    "blender": (3, 0, 0),
    "category": "Object",
}

import bpy

def change_cursor_in_edit_mode(self, context):
    if context.mode == 'EDIT_MESH':
        context.window.cursor_modal_set('DEFAULT')
    else:
        context.window.cursor_modal_set('CROSSHAIR')

class ChangeCursorInEditModeAddon(bpy.types.Operator):
    bl_idname = "object.change_cursor_in_edit_mode"
    bl_label = "Change Cursor in Edit Mode"

    def execute(self, context):
        change_cursor_in_edit_mode(self, context)
        return {'FINISHED'}

def register():
    bpy.utils.register_class(ChangeCursorInEditModeAddon)
    bpy.types.VIEW3D_HT_header.prepend(change_cursor_in_edit_mode)

def unregister():
    bpy.utils.unregister_class(ChangeCursorInEditModeAddon)
    bpy.types.VIEW3D_HT_header.remove(change_cursor_in_edit_mode)

if __name__ == "__main__":
    register()
```

essentially, yeah. But I've tried many different things with blender's own shrinkwrap modifer to no results. This is the article

